  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-11T10:17:07.540Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I can't invite myself to this public instance:\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_6caf5200-70e1-46c2-b043-e3c4abe69e0f&instanceId=ArcticLucky_AI~group%28grp_7c75c192-e00e-4ac8-a14b-95bcbfa8429b%29~groupAccessType%28public%29~region%28us%29\n\nShout-out to Nekromateion who figured out what is wrong: https://github.com/vrcx-team/VRCX/issues/767#issuecomment-2048547628\n\nThe (same) issue is present when you try to use the VRChat website to invite yourself to the instance.\n\nThe API request fails and returns a 400 error, but the website doesn't handle this and simply displays the checkmark regardless.\n\nThe endpoint that is used is (already in your original message so I figured you'd know).\n\n`/api/1/invite/myself/to/{WorldIdWithInstanceId}`\n\nThe endpoint attempts to validate the InstanceID but that filter only checks for alphanumerical and the \"_\" causes it to mark the InstanceID as invalid.",
